  'topic.start.s2.help': 'You received a temporary password: the portal asks you to choose a new one. Long passphrases are welcome; there is no composition rule and no periodic expiry. If your account requires two-step verification, you set it up right after.',
  'topic.start.s3.title': 'Two-step verification',
  'topic.start.s3.help': 'Scan the QR code with an authenticator app (or type the key), enter the first code and store the recovery codes offline: each one works once and lets you sign in if you lose the device. From then on, after the password the portal asks for the 6-digit code of the app.',
  'topic.start.s4.title': 'If you cannot sign in',
  'topic.start.s4.b1': 'Too many attempts: wait the seconds shown, then try again.',
  'topic.start.s4.b2': 'Lost device: choose "Use a recovery code instead".',
  'topic.start.s4.b3': 'Forgotten password or no recovery codes left: an administrator can reset your password or your two-step verification. If no administrator can sign in, a local administrator of the gateway server issues a one-time recovery token, to use with "Recover account" on the sign-in page.',
  'topic.start.layout': 'The screen',
  'topic.start.l.nav': 'Left panel',
  'topic.start.l.navText': 'the icons at the top open the main areas, such as Dashboard, Inventory, Networks, Storage, Templates, Tasks and Guide (Settings appears only to who manages users, roles or settings, or reads the audit log): hover an icon to read its name. Below them a tree follows the page: hosts, groups and VMs in the inventory, hosts and switches in Networks, statuses in Tasks. Drag its edge to resize it; the button at the top left hides it.',
  'topic.start.l.search': 'Search (Ctrl+K)',
  'topic.start.l.searchText': 'the box at the top, or Ctrl+K anywhere: type part of the name of a VM, host, group or page and press Enter. It also starts common actions, such as New virtual machine.',
  'topic.start.l.menu': 'Actions menus',
  'topic.start.l.menuText': 'right-click a VM, host or group in the tree or in a table (or use its ⋯ button): you get the same actions as the Actions button of its page. Only the actions you may perform now are listed.',
  'topic.start.l.tasksText': 'the panel at the bottom. Every change you request becomes a task: the panel shows the latest ones with their status, and a notice appears when a task you started from this window finishes. "All tasks" opens the full list.',
  'topic.start.l.live': 'Live indicator',
  'topic.start.l.liveText': 'the dot at the top right. Green: pages update by themselves (VM states, tasks). Amber: reconnecting. Grey: live updates are off and what you see may be old: reload the page.',
  'topic.start.l.account': 'Account menu',
  'topic.start.l.accountText': 'your initials at the top right: My account, language (Italiano / English), theme (System, Light, Dark) and Sign out. Language and theme are remembered by this browser.',
  'topic.start.views': 'Dashboard and inventory',
  'topic.start.v.dashText': 'connected hosts, running VMs, active tasks and the objects that need attention (for example a host offline or a VM missing from the latest inventory), with the latest tasks.',
  'topic.start.v.invText': 'the single entry point for hosts, groups and VMs, with the views Hosts, Groups (the folders of the portal and the VMs without a group) and All VMs. The tree has the same three sections; its Filter box searches the names (and the notes of the VMs).',
  'topic.start.v.stale': 'Old data',
